        "lifeEvents": "Born Maria Reveley, she and her first husband Willey Reveley belonged to the late-eighteenth-century English radical circle around Bentham and Godwin. In a March 1818 letter Godwin reminded her that the newborn Mary had been taken to her house and 'protected for a week' a very few days after birth. Widow of the architect Willey Reveley and mother of Henry Willey Reveley, she married John Gisborne in 1800 and settled in Italy. At Livorno and Pisa she became one of the Shelleys' closest Italian friends: Mary and Claire place the Gisborne household at the center of the Livorno-Pisa network, and the letters to Maria Gisborne preserve some of the richest documentary evidence for the Italian years."
