      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Shelley's Lake District residence is fixed by the surviving correspondence itself: the NYPL manuscript guide records letters to Hogg from Keswick on 14 November 1811 and from Chestnut Hill and Chestnut Cottage in the same district during the following month, while Letters to Godwin preserves the January 1812 Keswick letters that launch the Godwin correspondence from there. The DNB biography adds that in this winter 1811-1812 Keswick stay Shelley met with the kindest reception from Robert Southey, so Southey should be treated as a documented literary contact of the Keswick months beginning in November 1811.",
