      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "RCAHMW identifies the mapped house-site as Plas Tan yr Allt above Tremadog. The interruption of this first Tanyrallt phase by an autumn London stay is independently supported by Godwin's early October diary contacts with the Shelleys and by Hogg's 7 November 1812 St. James's Coffee-house letter, which shows Shelley still in London shortly before the resumed return to Tanyrallt. Walter Edwin Peck adds a further local function to this first stay: Shelley had scarcely settled into William Alexander Madocks's new villa before helping canvass subscriptions for the unfinished Tremadog embankment works.",
