      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": false,
      "summary": "The specific 11 October event remains slightly cautious because Godwin's diary records 'invites Shelleys' rather than a fully completed dinner formula. But the broader autumn London return is independently secure: the Godwin diary indexes Harriet Shelley and the Shelley household repeatedly on 4, 5, 6, 11, and 24 October 1812, and Hogg preserves Shelley's own 7 November 1812 letter from St. James's Coffee-house, proving that the party was in London through early November before returning to Tanyrallt. Florence Marshall goes further and says that on the last day of the October visit 'the Shelleys, with Eliza Westbrook, dined in Skinner Street'.",
