      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": false,
      "summary": "Garrett's Mary Shelley chronology places Shelley, Harriet Shelley, Eliza Westbrook, the Godwins, and Dr William Lawrence together at Skinner Street on 11 November 1812, the day after Mary Godwin returned from Scotland with Christy Baxter. Garrett treats the dinner as a likely first meeting between Shelley and Mary, while noting Seymour's stricter possibility that Mary stayed upstairs recovering from the journey, so the event is kept but not given high certainty.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": "This November 1812 dinner is one of the strongest candidates for Shelley's first face-to-face meeting with Mary Godwin, and it places Dr William Lawrence in the same Godwin scientific-medical orbit.",
