      "dateDisplay": "Returned to Tanyrallt in mid-Nov 1812; remained until departure via Bangor Ferry in early Mar 1813",
      "startDate": "1812-11-15",
      "endDate": "1813-03-05",
      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Shelley's Hogg letters from Tanyralt in December 1812 and February 1813 fix the household at Tan-yr-Allt itself, and Hogg also preserves Shelley's 7 November 1812 London letter announcing the immediate return to Tanyrallt. Jeaffreson's mid-November reconstruction is therefore corroborated by nearer evidence. This was also the scene of the so-called Tanyrallt assassination attempt on the stormy night of 26 February 1813: Shelley, Harriet, and later Eliza described an armed intruder and fired shots, while later biographers such as Garnett and Symonds stressed that the incident remains unresolved and may partly reflect hallucination or confused testimony rather than a clearly established murder plot.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": "On the night of 26 February 1813, Shelley said an intruder fired at him here; the disputed incident closed the resumed Tanyrallt stay, and the household was at Bangor Ferry by 6 March.",
