      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Jeaffreson says Shelley and Harriet were in Chapel Street, Grosvenor Square, by the second week of April 1813 after the return from Ireland, and treats No. 23 Chapel Street as the Westbrook family house used in that season. Shelley and His Circle sharpens the social and topographical setting by identifying John Westbrook at the same address in Boyle's Court Guide, and by connecting him with The Mount at 78-79 Lower Grosvenor Street and later the Poulterers' Arms in Freeman's Court off Cheapside. Jeaffreson also notes that Shelley gave 'No. 23, Chapel Street, Grosvenor Square, London' as the imprint address of the private 1813 Queen Mab edition.",
