      "summary": "After the Irish return, Shelley and Harriet are back in London by the second week of April 1813, when Jeaffreson places them in Chapel Street, Grosvenor Square. He then reconstructs the next months from postmarks and Hogg's recollections as a sequence involving Chapel Street, Cooke's Hotel, Half-Moon Street, and Pimlico, while Harriet's surviving 9 May 1813 note from Cooke's Hotel provides direct manuscript evidence within the same London phase.",
