      "summary": "Harriet Shelley's autograph note of 9 May 1813 is explicitly from 'Cooke's Hotel, Albemarle Street, Piccadilly,' and the NYPL also preserves a Shelley address-sheet from Cooke's Hotel. Jeaffreson argues that this was an address and interview point used across the London weeks, not necessarily the only residence. Clutton-Brock's narrative likewise places the Shelleys first at a hotel in Albemarle Street and only afterwards in later lodgings.",
