      "lifePeriodOrder": 3,
      "dateDisplay": "Documented London lodgings for several weeks in late spring 1813",
      "startDate": "1813-05-20",
      "endDate": "1813-06-20",
      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Hogg's own later memoir says that after the hurried return from Killarney Shelley and Harriet stayed first at a hotel in Dover Street and then took lodgings in Half-Moon Street for several months, where Shelley was visible all day in a projecting window with a book in hand. Jeaffreson, weighing postmarks and other evidence, reconstructs the same Half-Moon Street phase within the middle of April to middle of July 1813, while Mitton separately notes Shelley on Half-Moon Street in 1813. Clutton-Brock places the same phase inside the new Newton-Boinville acquaintance that was already reshaping Shelley's London social world.",
