      "dateDisplay": "Later London lodgings before the Berkshire move, summer 1813",
      "startDate": "1813-06-21",
      "endDate": "1813-07-26",
      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Hogg says that after the Half-Moon Street lodgings Shelley and Harriet 'went to Pimlico to be near the B.'s' and adds that he believed Harriet's first confinement took place there. Jeaffreson places the later spring-summer 1813 lodgings in Pimlico before the move to Bracknell, which fits Hogg's sequence. Clutton-Brock's account of the same months strengthens the social setting by placing Shelley in close intimacy with the Newton-Boinville circle immediately before the Berkshire move.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": "Hogg linked these later Pimlico lodgings with Harriet's first confinement and, probably, the birth phase of Ianthe Shelley.",
