      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Mary Shelley's journal shows Shelley with Peacock at Great Marlow by 15-16 September 1816, while the chronologies indicate that after landing at Portsmouth he first went to London on 9 September before shifting into the Marlow house-hunting phase. Mary left Bath on 19 September, met Shelley and Peacock at Maidenhead, and walked with them to Marlow; on 25 September she returned to Bath with Shelley. Great Marlow therefore marks the intermediate English base between the London business stop and the resumed Bath household.",
