      "endDateApproximate": false,
      "summary": "A Mary Shelley Chronology and A Shelley Chronology agree that after the landing at Portsmouth Shelley went first to London on 9 September 1816, chiefly to deliver Byron's manuscripts to John Murray and handle financial business, while Mary, Claire, William, and Elise travelled separately via Salisbury to Bath. This makes London the best-documented intermediate stop between Portsmouth and the Marlow phase, even though the surviving journal does not preserve a Percy dateline from the city on that day.",
