      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Mary Shelley's journal says that after an alarming letter from Skinner Street about Fanny, Shelley went immediately to Bristol and returned in the night without firm news; the editorial note further says that Shelley, like Godwin, had set out for Bristol to find Fanny. A later October entry adds that Shelley went again to Bristol and obtained a more certain trace. The place is therefore secure as a crisis-search destination, even though the exact sequence of hours and movements remains compressed in the journal and notes.",
