      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": false,
      "summary": "Marshall says that Shelley returned to Bath on 14 December 1816 and that on the next day Hookham's letter informed him that Harriet's body had been taken from the Serpentine. Rossetti retells the same Bath setting, while Mary Shelley's own Bath letter of 17 December confirms that Bath was still the household's base while Percy hurried to London over the children and Chancery. Clutton-Brock further reports that Harriet had moved shortly before her death to Queen Street, Brompton, while the children had been sent away to a clergyman at Warwick.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": "Here Shelley learned that Harriet had died and immediately turned to the question of recovering Ianthe and Charles.",
