      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Marlow is repeatedly attested in the correspondence; a surviving NYPL letter to Charles Ollier of 22 January 1818 is explicitly 'From Marlow,' while biographical summaries place the household's move there in March 1817. Byoung Chun Min's article on Shelley's 'Hermit of Marlow' pamphlets also treats the Marlow residence as the setting in which Shelley, now closely linked to Leigh Hunt's circle, produced the reform pamphlets A Proposal for Putting Reform to the Vote throughout the Kingdom and An Address to the People on the Death of the Princess Charlotte. Walter Edwin Peck preserves local Marlow recollections that Shelley was constantly on the river here and that his boat was known as 'Vaga', later chalk-pranked into 'Vagabond'.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": null,
      "travelMode": null,
      "routeNote": null,
      "certainty": "high",
