      "summary": "Shelley's letter of 5 June 1818 is headed from Livorno and says the family had remained there about a month after the Pisa crossing. Mary Shelley's journal and Frederick L. Jones's Maria Gisborne letters article show that this first Livorno month was also the period of renewed contact with Maria Gisborne and Henry Reveley; on 28 May Mary records an evening walk to see Henry Reveley's steam engine, and John White's 1976 Reveley study says Shelley later invested 200 pounds in Henry's projected commercial steamboat for the Leghorn-Genoa-Marseilles trade.",
