      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Mary Shelley's journal records the move on 11 July 1818: 'Travel to the Bagni di Lucca and settle ourselves a little in our house,' and the scholarly note to the journal identifies that house as Casa Bertini. Shelley Memorials then preserves Mary Shelley's own June 1818 letter from 'Casa Bertini, Bagni di Lucca', describing the small but commodious house, its laurel arbour, and the domestic arrangements there. Both sources also identify Signor Chiappa as the owner of Casa Bertini. The later Bagni plaque at Piazza Edoardo Tolomei 2 preserves the same building-name tradition.",
