      "summary": "Mary Shelley's journal records the move on 7 May 1819: 'Change our lodgings,' and the editorial note identifies the new address precisely as 65 Via Sistina, next door to Miss Curran at 64. Palazzo Zuccari occupies the corner complex between Via Sistina and Via Gregoriana at Trinita dei Monti, so the Shelley lodging can be mapped to the palace's residential wing while preserving the historically attested Via Sistina address. Mary herself wrote on 11 May that they had moved to 'the Trinita dei Monti', confirming the same upper-Rome quarter as the family's final Roman lodging before departure.",
