      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Donald Reiman and Michael O'Neill's manuscript study states that Sophia Stacey and Miss Corbet Parry-Jones arrived in Florence in November 1819, shared the same Via Valfonda boarding-house with the Shelleys from 11 November, and left for Rome on 29 December with Shelley's letter of introduction to Signora Marianna Dionigi. Valentina Varinelli's reconstruction of the Florence months aligns with that picture, while Shelley's letter to the Gisbornes from Florence on 23 December 1819 confirms that the household was still in the city at the end of this stay.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": "Sophia Stacey suggested the newborn's middle name 'Florence' during this Via Valfonda stay, and Shelley used the same lodgings as the base from which he recommended her into Marianna Candidi Dionigi's Roman salon circle.",
