      "summary": "Claire Clairmont's journal says that after travelling from Pisa to Florence with Shelley on 20 October 1820, she went the next day with Signor Tantini to 'Casa Bojti — opposite Palazzo Pitti', where Shelley took leave of her in the evening. The journal's Appendix C identifies Dr. Antonio Bojti as the Florentine physician in whose household Claire stayed as a paying guest and places the house in the same block opposite Palazzo Pitti later associated with Casa Guidi. This gives one clear Percy-linked Florence stop in the Bojti household, even though the exact modern frontage remains uncertain.",
