      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": false,
      "summary": "Claire Clairmont's journal fixes the acquaintance one day earlier than the old summary wording implied: on the evening of 1 December 1820 Pacchiani, Sgricci, and Esopo sup with the household, and Sgricci improvises on the future independence of Italy. Shelley himself then writes from Pisa to Claire on 18 February 1821 that he is 'provoked at Sgricci's assumption', proving a direct personal connection in the same Pisan phase. Symonds and Jeaffreson both keep Sgricci among the notable figures of Shelley's Pisa circle, while Medwin's Pisa recollections independently preserve Pacchiani as a central intermediary in the same social world.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": null,
