      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Teresa ('Emilia') Viviani was confined in Sant'Anna, and the Pisa residences survey places Shelley's attempts to meet her there between 3 December 1820 and 2 April 1821. Mary Shelley's recollections confirm that Mary and Claire first saw the 'lovely captive' before Shelley's own attachment deepened into the Epipsychidion episode, while Medwin and Clutton-Brock both preserve the Pisan tradition that Pacchiani first described Emilia's beauty and led Shelley into the convent parlour context. Pisa Tours identifies the surviving church and former cenobio on Via Carducci.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": "Teresa ('Emilia') Viviani, the addressee of Epipsychidion, was confined here.",
      "travelMode": null,
      "routeNote": null,
