      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": false,
      "summary": "The secure Pugnano residence of Edward and Jane Williams is the villa of the Marchese Poschi. Mary Shelley's journal note to 5 April 1821 says that after house-hunting at Pugnano the Williamses later took the villa of the Marchese Poschi there; Garrett's chronology then makes the occupation explicit from 8 May, when Mary and Prince Mavrocordato go to Pugnano to see the Williamses, and Claire Clairmont's journal shows that she stayed with the Williamses at Pugnano from 11 to 30 October 1821. The current Villa Poschi site at Pugnano preserves the Poschi name and presents the house as the family's eighteenth-century summer villa.",
