      "summary": "Shelley's letter to Mary from Ravenna on 7 August 1821 says he arrived the previous night and sat up with Byron until five in the morning, making Byron's residence the obvious setting of the visit. The introduction to The Ravenna Journal says Byron rented from Count Guiccioli a floor in Palazzo Guiccioli on Via Porta Adriana, now Via Cavour, and notes that it was in those apartments that Shelley visited him. Byron's own published letters and journals preserve the same household context, while Ravenna Citta del Mosaico identifies Palazzo Guiccioli at Via Cavour 54 as the palace where Byron lived from 1819 to 1821.",
