      "lifePeriodId": "pisan_circle",
      "lifePeriodLabel": "Pisan circle and final months",
      "lifePeriodOrder": 9,
      "dateDisplay": "Upper-floor apartment on Lungarno Galilei from late Oct 1821 into spring 1822",
      "startDate": "1821-10-25",
      "endDate": "1822-04-30",
      "startDateApproximate": false,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Claire Clairmont's journal gives the transition back into Pisa in unusually exact terms: on 27 October 1821 she goes from Pugnano into Pisa 'to the tre Palazzi di Chiesa', and on 31 October she is fetched there again after passing through Casa Silva. Mary Shelley's 30 November 1821 letter then says that the household was living 'at the top of the Tre Palazzi di Chiesa' on the Lung'Arno, with Lord Byron just opposite in Casa Lanfranchi. The Liberal Project identifies this as the apartment rented on the Shelleys' return from Bagni di Pisa in October 1821, and the Comune di Pisa now preserves the site under the name Palazzo Chiesa.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": null,
      "travelMode": null,
