      "summary": "Symonds, drawing on Trelawny, says that after mornings spent reading and sailing on the Arno Shelley regularly went to 'the pine-forest' and that 'the great wood of stone pines on the Pisan Maremma was his favourite study'. Trelawny adds the anecdote of finding Shelley there alone with the manuscript of Ariel to Miranda. The modern marker uses the San Rossore pinewood access point at Cascine Vecchie as a practical anchor for the wider Pisan Maremma landscape.",
