      "summary": "Mary Shelley's journal records an evening walk with the Gisbornes and Henry Reveley 'to Mrs Partridge', and the editors identify Mrs. Partridge as an aunt of Benjamin Robert Haydon who lived at Montenero, not far from Leghorn. Later Livorno topography and the Livorno delle Nazioni article make it plausible that the Partridge family house was the villa later known as Villa Ombrosa, which Italian architectural history still records as a property once owned by the Partridge family; but the exact identification of Mrs. Partridge's 1822 house with the surviving villa remains probable rather than fully closed.",
