      "country": "Italy",
      "modernAddress": "Lungarno Mediceo 17, Pisa",
      "historicalState": "Grand Duchy of Tuscany (Granducato di Toscana)",
      "relationType": "visited",
      "relationGroup": "visited",
      "lifePeriodId": "pisan_circle",
      "lifePeriodLabel": "Pisan circle and final months",
      "lifePeriodOrder": 9,
      "dateDisplay": "1-2 Jul 1822, Shelley brought the Hunts into Byron's Pisa palace",
      "startDate": "1822-07-01",
      "endDate": "1822-07-02",
      "startDateApproximate": true,
      "endDateApproximate": true,
      "summary": "Symonds says that after hearing of Leigh Hunt's arrival in Genoa, Shelley sailed with Edward Williams to Leghorn on 1 July 1822, then drove with the Hunt family to Pisa and established them in the ground-floor of Byron's Palazzo Lanfranchi. William Harvey Marshall's dissertation on The Liberal sharpens that sequence, placing Hunt's arrival at Genoa on 15 June, his move toward Leghorn on 28 June, and Shelley's transfer of the family into the palace on 3 July. The 1928 Shelley-Leigh Hunt documentary narrative preserves Shelley's practical Leghorn instructions to Hunt, including shipment via 'Mr. Guebhard, Merchant, Leghorn' and the advice to embark direct for Leghorn, which supports the Leghorn-to-Pisa logistics of the same July crisis. Mary Shelley's printed letter account says that on arriving at Pisa Shelley sent for Vacca, who judged Marianne Hunt desperately ill and explained the treatment to Leigh Hunt. The palace thus became not only Byron's Pisa residence but also the Hunts' first Pisan lodging under Shelley's care and the place where Andrea Vacca entered their story.",
      "inscription": null,
      "importantFact": "Shelley personally brought Leigh Hunt and Marianne Hunt from Leghorn to Pisa, settled them here, and summoned Andrea Vacca to examine Marianne Hunt.",
      "travelMode": null,
      "routeNote": null,
      "certainty": "high",
      "works": [
        "The Liberal"
      ],
      "companions": [
        "Leigh Hunt",
        "Marianne Hunt",
        "Andrea Vacca Berlinghieri"
      ],
      "companionsNote": "This brief July 1822 record marks Shelley's settling of the Hunt household into Byron's palace and summoning Andrea Vacca to see Marianne Hunt.",
