      "endDateApproximate": false,
      "summary": "The sculpture was created by Christopher Kelly in 1988 as part of the Powys Sculpture Trail. Inspired by 'Prometheus Unbound', it comprises five bronze figures on a circular slate plinth. The central figure is Shelley deep in creative thought, flanked by nymph-like female figures representing the poet's muse. Kelly began preparatory work during a three-month residency at the Elan Valley Visitor Centre in 1986. The trail was developed by the Welsh Sculpture Trust and Powys County Council.",
