      "summary": "Comune di Pisa states that on the last surviving ruined wall of Palazzo Chiesa one reads, on an epigraph, the name of Percy Bysshe Shelley, and that the plaque was placed in memory of the stay of Percy and Mary Shelley. The Accademia dei Disuniti event archive documents the present marble plaque ceremony at Pisa on 29 June 2018, which is the firm date now attached to the surviving memorial marker on Lungarno Galilei. The fuller history of earlier Palazzo Chiesa memorial stones remains under separate verification.",
